@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+Feature: Todo Editing
+  As a user
+  I want to edit existing todo titles
+  So that I can correct or update task descriptions
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is open
+    And I have a todo named "Buy groceries"
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a todo label activates editing mode
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo should have class "editing"
+    And an edit input should be visible containing "Buy groceries"
+
+  Scenario: Editing is saved on blur
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy groceries"
+    And I change the edit input value to "Buy milk"
+    And I tab away (blur) from the edit input
+    Then I should see a todo item labeled "Buy milk"
+    And the todo should not have class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Editing is saved on Enter
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy groceries"
+    And I change the edit input value to "Buy milk"
+    And I press Enter
+    Then I should see a todo item labeled "Buy milk"
+    And the todo should not have class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Empty edit destroys the todo
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy groceries"
+    And I clear the edit input
+    And I press Enter
+    Then the todo list should be empty
+
+  Scenario: Escape cancels editing and restores the original title
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy groceries"
+    And I change the edit input value to "Buy milk"
+    And I press Escape
+    Then I should see a todo item labeled "Buy groceries"
+    And the todo should not have class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Destroy button removes a todo
+    When I click the destroy button for "Buy groceries"
+    Then the todo list should be empty
