@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+Feature: Todo Persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to be saved across page reloads
+  So that I don't lose my task list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is open
+
+  Scenario: Todos are persisted to localStorage
+    When I create a todo named "Buy groceries"
+    And I create a todo named "Walk the dog"
+    Then localStorage should contain a key matching "todos-"
+    And the stored value should include a todo with title "Buy groceries"
+    And the stored value should include a todo with title "Walk the dog"
+
+  Scenario: Completed state is persisted
+    When I create a todo named "Buy groceries"
+    And I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy groceries"
+    Then the stored value for "Buy groceries" should have completed set to true
+
+  Scenario: Editing state is not persisted
+    When I create a todo named "Buy groceries"
+    And I double-click the label for "Buy groceries"
+    Then the stored value for "Buy groceries" should not have an "editing" property
+
+  Scenario: Todos survive page reload
+    When I create a todo named "Buy groceries"
+    And I reload the app
+    Then I should see a todo item labeled "Buy groceries" in the list
+
+  Scenario: Active filter is persisted on reload
+    When I navigate to "#/active"
+    And I reload the app
+    Then the filter link for "Active" should have class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Stored todo items have id, title, and completed keys
+    When I create a todo named "Buy groceries"
+    Then each stored todo item should have an "id" property
+    And each stored todo item should have a "title" property
+    And each stored todo item should have a "completed" property
\ No newline at end of file
