@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+Feature: Todo Counter and Routing
+  As a user
+  I want to see how many active todos remain and filter the list
+  So that I can focus on what needs attention
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is open
+    And I have the following todos:
+      | title          |
+      | Buy groceries  |
+      | Walk the dog   |
+      | Write report   |
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows the number of active todos
+    Given the todo "Buy groceries" is completed
+    Then the todo-count should display "2"
+    And it should read "2 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter uses singular "item" for one active todo
+    Given the todo "Buy groceries" is completed
+    And the todo "Walk the dog" is completed
+    Then the todo-count should display "1"
+    And it should read "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Routing shows all todos by default
+    When I navigate to "#/"
+    Then I should see 3 todos in the list
+
+  Scenario: Active filter shows only active todos
+    Given the todo "Buy groceries" is completed
+    When I navigate to "#/active"
+    Then I should see 2 todos in the list
+    And I should not see a todo named "Buy groceries"
+
+  Scenario: Completed filter shows only completed todos
+    Given the todo "Buy groceries" is completed
+    When I navigate to "#/completed"
+    Then I should see 1 todo in the list
+    And the todo name should be "Buy groceries"
+
+  Scenario: Filter link gets selected class for current route
+    When I navigate to "#/active"
+    Then the filter link for "Active" should have class "selected"
+    And the filter link for "All" should not have class "selected"
+    And the filter link for "Completed" should not have class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Updating a todo while filtered re-filters it accordingly
+    Given the todo "Buy groceries" is completed
+    And I am viewing the Active filter
+    When I click the toggle checkbox for "Walk the dog"
+    Then I should not see a todo named "Walk the dog" in the list
